================================================================================
SECTION 3 — INTEGRATION NOTES THAT ARE EASY TO GET WRONG
================================================================================

1. CRATE PATH. `dimabot/src/lib.rs` exposes `domain_events/mod.rs` as
   `domain_event_contracts`. The real path for the wave 2-A module tree is
   therefore `crate::domain_event_contracts::polar_billing::…` —
   NOT `crate::domain_events::…`. Every team1 file and test already uses the
   correct path; a rename in src/lib.rs would break all of them.

2. `definitions()` STAYS AT 42 ENTRIES. Both new schema modules are
   feature-gated `#[path]` declarations and are deliberately NOT appended to
   the `definitions()` array. This is contract tl1-c3, agreed with the
   integration team. Appending them would change a central registry that other
   teams also depend on.

3. GOLDEN CONSUMERS MUST FAIL, NEVER SKIP (contract tl1-c5). Every team1
   oracle consumer hard-fails on a missing, unreadable, empty, or invalid
   golden. There is no `Ok(())` and no skip path. A red result on a missing
   golden is the CORRECT behaviour, not a test bug. Oracles run only in the
   pinned Node 24.22.1 image (`sha256:a001f865dc47694124ef59a1f71cdf80e6214f64613f4e5b4d891088f71dca82`)
   via `validate.py`; host Node must not run them. Pins are unchanged.

4. OPEN DEPENDENCY — tl1-c4. `applyPolarRewardDomainEvent` depends on
   `applyPaidOrderReward` from `src/utils/paid_order_reward.ts`, which is
   team2's file and is NOT natively ported. The filters and validation are
   implemented; the branch has no concrete adapter and is NOT shippable.
   This is deliberately left open — do not close it by inventing an adapter.

5. OPEN DEPENDENCY — the PolarGiftAcceptor seam. `polar_billing::PolarGiftAcceptor`
   has no concrete adapter until team1's wave 3-A lands
   `src/utils/credit_gifts.rs` with an implementation. The gift branch of
   `apply_credit_gift_domain_event` is not shippable until then.

6. OPEN DEPENDENCY — `src/utils/ai_usage_backfill.rs`
   (`syncAiUsageBackfillJob`). It needs `fetchAiUsageTransactions`, which
   lives in lane B's `src/utils/ai_usage_period.rs`. Wave 3-C was explicitly
   instructed NOT to author it, to avoid a second copy and a cross-lane Rust
   dependency. It stays blocked until lane B lands that module.

7. HTTP WEBHOOK ROUTE. The Polar webhook HTTP route and its raw-body
   middleware are central (`src/lib.rs`). team1 delivered the pure signature
   verifier and the exact response bodies; the route wiring is the
   integration team's.

8. DISK HEADROOM. `/dev/sda1` was at 5.8G free against a 5GiB floor at the
   time of writing. team1 pruned nothing and owns no cache. team1's own
   footprint is small (src ~14M, tests ~29M). Cleanup is integration-owned.

